{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "grp-stage1",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "STAGE 1 | Multi-Sensor Ingestion & Cross-Calibration",
      "x": -1360,
      "y": -440,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 1100,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage1-calib",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83d\udce1 STAGE 1A | Multi-Sensor Calibration\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[cookbooks/11-multi-sensor-cross-calibration/README|Open Cookbook 11 Playbook \u2197]]**\n\n### System Inputs & Kinematics\n- **RGB Camera**: 4K 60 FPS pinhole stream ($f_x = 800, f_y = 800$)\n- **Thermal Imager**: Long-Wave Infrared (LWIR) $640 \\times 512$\n- **LiDAR**: 32-beam solid-state / spinning point cloud ($50\\text{ m}$)\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n- **Algorithm**: Closed-form Horn Procrustes SVD rigid transform\n- **Objective**: Recovers optimal $(R, t) \\in SE(3)$ between sensor frames\n- **Parallax Correction**: Sub-pixel metric depth projection\n- **Precision**: $< 0.05^\\circ$ angular rotation error, $< 1.0\\text{ mm}$ translation",
      "x": -1320,
      "y": -380,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage1-fusion",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83d\udd00 STAGE 1B | Sensor Fusion Strategy\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[topics/sensor-fusion/00-sensor-fusion-moc|Open Sensor Fusion Domain MOC \u2197]]**\n\n### Architectural Trade-offs\n- **Early Fusion**: Raw pixel + point concatenation (sensitive to calibration drift)\n- **Late Fusion**: Track-to-track association (high latency, misses weak signals)\n- **Asymmetric BEV Fusion**: Feature-level cross-attention (SOTA)\n\n### Benchmark & Production Guide\n- **Standard**: NuScenes Validation ($72.9\\%\\text{ NDS}$, $68.4\\%\\text{ mAP}$)\n- **Guide**: [[topics/sensor-fusion/README|Production Sensor Fusion Playbook]]",
      "x": -1320,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 310,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage1-thor",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \u26a1 COMPUTE | NVIDIA DRIVE Thor\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[hardware/nvidia-drive-thor|Open Silicon Architecture Reference \u2197]]**\n\n### Hardware Specification\n- **Throughput**: 2,000 FP8 TFLOPS @ 300 W Automotive SoC\n- **Architecture**: Blackwell Tensor Cores + ARM Neoverse V3AE\n- **Safety Islands**: Dual-core lockstep for ISO 26262 ASIL-D\n- **Memory**: Unified LPDDR5X (>1 TB/s memory bandwidth)\n- **Role**: Centralized autonomous driving perception & control",
      "x": -1320,
      "y": 330,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 290,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "grp-stage2",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "STAGE 2 | 2D Camera & 3D LiDAR Feature Extraction",
      "x": -680,
      "y": -440,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 1100,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage2-rfdetr",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83c\udfaf STAGE 2A | Real-Time 2D Detection\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[cookbooks/01-rfdetr-tensorrt/README|Open Cookbook 01 Playbook \u2197]]**\n\n### Detection Model Specification\n- **Model**: RF-DETR (DINOv2 Backbone + SuperNet NAS)\n- **Engine**: TensorRT 10 FP16 compiled engine (`rf_detr.engine`)\n- **Performance**: $56.9\\%\\text{ AP}$ on COCO @ $1.15\\text{ ms}$ (RTX 4090)\n- **Memory**: Zero-copy page-locked host/device pinned memory\n- **Production Guide**: [[topics/object-detection/README|Object Detection Playbook]]",
      "x": -640,
      "y": -380,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage2-yolov10",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f ARCHITECTURE | YOLOv10 Dual-Label\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[architectures/real-time-detectors-and-segmenters/yolov10|Open Architecture Deep-Dive \u2197]]**\n\n### Model Innovation\n- **NMS-Free Training**: Dual label assignment eliminates non-maximum suppression\n- **Efficiency**: Rank-guided block aggregation reduces redundant convolutions\n- **Large-Kernel Convolutions**: $7 \\times 7$ depthwise filters expand receptive field\n- **Latency Benchmark**: $1.84\\text{ ms}$ end-to-end on Jetson AGX Orin\n- **License**: AGPL-3.0 / Commercial License Available",
      "x": -640,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 310,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage2-lidar",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \u2601\ufe0f STAGE 2B | 3D LiDAR Point Cloud Encoders\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[architectures/3d-pointclouds-and-lidar/pointpillars|PointPillars Architecture \u2197]]**\n\n### LiDAR Processing Pipeline\n- **Encoders**: PointPillars (2D Pseudo-images) & DSVT Voxel Transformers\n- **Input**: $(N, 4)$ LiDAR coordinates $[x, y, z, \\text{intensity}]$\n- **Voxelization**: Pillar feature net with $0.16\\text{ m} \\times 0.16\\text{ m}$ grid\n- **Latency**: $12.5\\text{ ms}$ on Jetson AGX Orin ($78.9\\%\\text{ mAP}$)\n- **Production Guide**: [[topics/lidar-perception/README|LiDAR Perception Playbook]]",
      "x": -640,
      "y": 330,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 290,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "grp-stage3",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "STAGE 3 | Spatial Bird's-Eye-View (BEV) Unification",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -440,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 1100,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage3-bevpool",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f STAGE 3A | Frustum Camera-to-BEV Pooling\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[cookbooks/14-bev-voxel-pooling-projection/README|Open Cookbook 14 Playbook \u2197]]**\n\n### Projection Mechanics (Lift-Splat-Shoot)\n- **Lift**: Generates $32\\text{k}$ frustum rays over 16 depth bins ($1.0\\text{--}50.0\\text{ m}$)\n- **Unproject**: Inverts intrinsics $K^{-1}$ and applies $[R_{\\text{cam2ego}} \\mid t_{\\text{cam2ego}}]$\n- **Splat**: Discretizes points into $128 \\times 128$ metric BEV spatial grid cells\n- **Voxel Pooling**: Fast cumulative segmented reduction without slow 3D convs\n- **Throughput**: $4.2\\text{ ms}$ ($238\\text{ FPS}$ on edge GPU)",
      "x": 40,
      "y": -380,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage3-bevfusion",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f ARCHITECTURE | MIT BEVFusion\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[architectures/3d-pointclouds-and-lidar/bevfusion|Open Architecture Reference \u2197]]**\n\n### Unified BEV Representation\n- **Multi-Modal Fusion**: Dual-branch camera & LiDAR feature map concatenation\n- **Precomputed Hash**: Accelerates camera-to-BEV pooling by $40\\times$\n- **Memory Footprint**: Only $0.4\\text{ GB}$ VRAM (vs. $1.8\\text{ GB}$ in vanilla LSS)\n- **Benchmark**: $72.9\\%\\text{ NDS}$ on nuScenes 3D detection test\n- **License**: Apache-2.0 Commercial Safe",
      "x": 40,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 310,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage3-bevgrid",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83d\udccc BEV SPATIAL SPECIFICATIONS\n\n### Coordinate Frame & Grids\n- **Ego Frame**: Forward $+X$, Left $+Y$, Up $+Z$\n- **Grid Dimensions**: $128 \\times 128$ cells ($64$ feature channels)\n- **Resolution**: $\\Delta x = 0.50\\text{ m}, \\Delta y = 0.50\\text{ m}$ per cell\n- **Spatial Coverage**: $[-32.0\\text{ m}, +32.0\\text{ m}] \\times [-32.0\\text{ m}, +32.0\\text{ m}]$\n- **Downstream Targets**: 3D Oriented Bounding Boxes & HD Map Semantic Lanes",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 330,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 290,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "grp-stage4",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "STAGE 4 | Multi-Object Tracking & 6-DoF Pose Estimation",
      "x": 680,
      "y": -440,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 1100,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage4-bytetrack",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83c\udfc3 STAGE 4A | ByteTrack Two-Stage Association\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[cookbooks/12-bytetrack-two-stage-association/README|Open Cookbook 12 Playbook \u2197]]**\n\n### Association Paradigm\n- **Stage 1**: Matches high-confidence detections ($s \\ge 0.60$) via IoU distance\n- **Stage 2**: Matches low-confidence candidates ($0.10 \\le s < 0.60$) to remaining tracks\n- **Occlusion Robustness**: Eliminates ID switches caused by transient occlusions\n- **Latency**: $0.35\\text{ ms}$ per frame ($3,570\\text{ FPS}$ association)\n- **Production Guide**: [[topics/video-tracking/README|Video Tracking Playbook]]",
      "x": 720,
      "y": -380,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage4-botsort",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f ARCHITECTURE | BoT-SORT & Kalman\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[architectures/visual-tracking-and-flow/bytetrack|Open Architecture Reference \u2197]]**\n\n### Tracking Mechanics\n- **Motion Model**: Constant velocity Kalman filter with covariance tuning\n- **Camera Motion Compensation (GMC)**: Affine transformation alignment\n- **Tracking Benchmark**: $80.3\\%\\text{ MOTA}$, $77.3\\%\\text{ IDF1}$ on MOT17\n- **Track Pool**: Zero-allocation preallocated track buffer (zero heap jitter)",
      "x": 720,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 310,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage4-epnp",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83d\udcd0 STAGE 4B | EPnP 6-DoF Analytical Solver\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[cookbooks/13-epnp-analytical-pose-solver/README|Open Cookbook 13 Playbook \u2197]]**\n\n### Closed-Form 6-DoF Pose Recovery\n- **Algorithm**: $\\mathcal{O}(n)$ Perspective-n-Point analytical SVD solver\n- **Virtual Control Points**: 4 Non-coplanar PCA points in barycentric coords\n- **Euclidean Distance Invariance**: Solves quadratic system for scale weights\n- **Performance**: $0.18\\text{ ms}$ execution ($5,500\\text{ FPS}$), zero local minima\n- **Production Guide**: [[topics/6dof-pose-estimation/README|6-DoF Pose Playbook]]",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 330,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 290,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "grp-stage5",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "STAGE 5 | Mission-Critical Safety Verification & ASIL-D",
      "x": 1360,
      "y": -440,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 1100,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage5-cbf",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f STAGE 5A | Control Barrier Filter (CBF-QP)\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[cookbooks/08-control-barrier-filter/README|Open Cookbook 08 Playbook \u2197]]**\n\n### Forward Invariance Enforcement\n- **Safety Invariant**: Nagumo condition $\\dot{h}(x) \\ge -\\alpha h(x)$ guarantees safe set $\\mathcal{C}$\n- **Quadratic Program**: $\\min \\frac{1}{2} \\|u - u_{\\text{deep}}\\|^2$ subject to $\\nabla h \\cdot u \\ge -\\alpha h$\n- **Intervention**: Solves closed-form KKT in $<50\\ \\mu\\text{s}$ to filter unsafe actions\n- **Application**: Overrides deep neural policy when collision is physically imminent\n- **Production Guide**: [[topics/safety-verification-and-robustness/README|Safety Playbook]]",
      "x": 1400,
      "y": -380,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage5-dann",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83d\udea8 STAGE 5B | Sim2Real Critical Safety Gate\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[cookbooks/09-dann-sim2real-safety-gate/README|Open Cookbook 09 Playbook \u2197]]**\n\n### Out-of-Distribution Monitoring\n- **Detection**: Mahalanobis latent domain discrepancy monitoring\n- **Adversarial Adaptation**: Gradient reversal alignment on synthetic training\n- **Safety Gate**: Triggers deterministic fail-safe state on anomaly\n- **Catch Rate**: $99.4\\%$ out-of-distribution synthetic anomalies caught\n- **Latency**: $0.12\\text{ ms}$ continuous statistical boundary check",
      "x": 1400,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 310,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-stage5-r52",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## \ud83d\udd12 HARDWARE | ARM Cortex-R52 Lockstep\n> \ud83d\udd17 **[[hardware/arm-cortex-r52|Open Safety Hardware Reference \u2197]]**\n\n### ISO 26262 ASIL-D Processor\n- **Architecture**: Dual-core lockstep with hardware comparator logic\n- **Fault Reaction**: Sub-microsecond deterministic fault recovery\n- **Memory Protection**: Hardware virtualization and MPU memory isolation\n- **Role**: Executes the CBF-QP safety filter independent of Linux OS",
      "x": 1400,
      "y": 330,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 290,
      "color": "1"
    }
  ],
